<p>Hello Candace,<br />
<br />
Thank you so much for your interest in sponsoring &nbsp;blood drives through the American Red Cross. &nbsp;As Hurricanes Harvey, Irma, Maria and the tragedy in Las Vegas have&nbsp;shown, it is the blood on the shelves that is critical to meet the needs across the country.&nbsp; Every 2 seconds someone needs blood.&nbsp; We work hard to replenish the supply every single day of the year.</p>

<p>To start, please look at the two attachments. The first one is our Blood Drive Interest Survey. This is to determine what sort of interest you have at your location for donating, and it will help us decide on a goal for your drive. &nbsp;We look for 30 names before we can confirm a date together for your drive. The second attachment is our Successful Blood Drive Guide. This is a simplified, step-by-step guide for success.</p>

<p>Once we determine there is sufficient interest and a time frame, I would need to come out to your location to view where you&nbsp;would be holding the drive to do a site check, as well as to give you some additional information about sponsoring a blood drive. I would only need about thirty&nbsp;minutes of your time.<br />
<br />
I will be in touch with you in a few days to see what sort of interest you have, and then we can proceed with looking at dates. In the meantime, please let me know if you have any questions.<br />
<br />
Thank you!</p>
Ann M. Wells<br />
